## Signature

- Provided by: **Claude Opus 5 (anthropic/claude-opus-5)** — 2026-10-08
- Method: fresh public internet research only. Sources that returned usable specification data: Moonshot's **Kimi Code "What's New"** changelog (the 2026-09-11 K2.8 Preview release entry — unchanged `kimi-for-coding` model ID, the three unquantified capability claims, the low/high/max thinking ladder with `max` default, the non-thinking fallback routing for the K3 series, and 1M context across all membership tiers; plus the quantified K2.7 Code and K3 entries used only for contrast), the **Kimi API model-pricing page** (which lists K3, K2.7 Code, K2.7 Code Highspeed and K2.6 but **not** K2.8 Preview, establishing that no per-token rate exists), and **LLM Stats** (release date, proprietary licence, Text/Image/Video input → Text output, 1M context, and blank Speed/Cost fields). Searches that returned nothing: `"Kimi K2.8" SWE-bench OR Terminal-Bench OR "Kimi Code Bench" score benchmark result` → **"No results found"**; BenchLM's model directory → **no K2.8 entry** despite eight sibling Moonshot models being indexed; Artificial Analysis → no entry. The repo's own `meta.json` was read only to identify the tracked model; its omission of video input is corrected above, and its "no per-token billing" note is confirmed correct. No benchmark was imported from `kimi-k2.7-code`, `kimi-k2.7-code-highspeed` or `kimi-k3`, and no value was interpolated between them. No peer `model/` findings files were read. Unavailable items — every benchmark figure, the parameter count, the architecture, the max output limit, the knowledge cutoff and any price — are recorded as "no verified public data found" rather than estimated.
- Future sources: add a new file next to this one, e.g. `GPT_5.md`, using the same headings.
